# AGENTS.md

@DESCRIPTION@

## Agent files stay out of git

- This file (`AGENTS.md`) and every other agent file stay untracked: `.AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`,
  `CLAUDE.local.md`, `GEMINI.md`, `.claude/`, `.cursor/`, `.cursorrules`, `.windsurfrules`,
  `.clinerules`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `.pi/`.
- The owner's global gitignore ignores them, and the repository's `.gitignore` does too, for other
  machines and CI.
- Never `git add -f` them. Never add an exception (`!AGENTS.md`) to `.gitignore`, and never remove
  them from it. Never mention them in the README or in commit messages as files of the project.
- If one shows up in `git status` or in a diff, stop and report it; do not commit it.

## Rules

- Work on a branch and open a PR; never merge, and never release. The owner decides.
- Commits and PR titles are Conventional Commits.
- Do not edit `CHANGELOG.md`, versions or `.release-please-manifest.json`; release-please does that.
- Do not weaken a check to make it pass.

## Checks

- `devenv shell -- check`
